AB  - The partnership between universities and industry is essential to promoting innovation and stimulating economic growth in today׳s knowledge-based economies. This contribution explores the complex dynamics of UIC (university-industry cooperation), emphasizing the intermediaries׳ crucial role. Based on an extensive examination of the current research, we examine different kinds of intermediates and how they contribute to and improve UIC. Our analysis highlights the diverse range of UIC intermediates, from industrial associations to technology transfer offices, all of which uniquely contribute to the link between industry and academia. In addition, we list and classify 22 tasks carried out by these actors, identifying their varied roles in networking, commercialization, IP protection, and information distribution. Understanding the institutional nature of UIC linkages impacts policymaking and interested parties by highlighting the significance of utilizing intermediary frameworks to maximize partnerships between the university and industry.
